    bottomLine: "For a desk walker of average build who wants a full-width belt and a long frame warranty for well under half the Unsit’s price.",
    description: "The TR1200Pro Glow-Up is LifeSpan’s long-running office treadmill in its current form. LifeSpan lists a 20 by 48-inch belt, a speed range of 0.4 to 4.0 mph that can be capped at 2 mph, a 330 lb maximum user weight, a 0.59-inch phenolic deck, a 4.6-inch step-up at the belt and six hours of recommended daily use, with 10 years on the frame, two on parts and one on labour. Its spec table and feature list give different motor descriptions, so neither is printed here. On 5 November 2026 LifeSpan listed it at $1,199, down from $1,299, as a pre-order.",
  },
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Brands", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/brands/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "InMovement Treadmill Desk", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/inmovement-treadmill-desk/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is InMovement the same company as iMovR?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "No. InMovement makes the Unsit treadmill and provides its warranty, servicing and technical support. iMovR is a separate retailer that sells the Unsit alongside its own standing desks. On 5 November 2026 InMovement also sold the Unsit direct from its own store.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much does the InMovement Unsit treadmill desk cost?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "On 5 November 2026 InMovement listed the Unsit treadmill at $2,595, its Unsit Standing Desk at $825, and the two as a bundle at $3,215 against a $3,420 reference price. iMovR listed the treadmill at $2,595 too. Curbside delivery was free from both. Prices change often.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What are the InMovement Unsit specifications?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "InMovement and iMovR agree on a 30 by 40-inch walking surface, 0.3 to 2.0 mph, a 400 lb maximum user weight, a 5-inch step-up, a 162 lb unit weight and a lifetime frame, two-year parts and one-year labour warranty. The motor is given as 2.75 HP by InMovement and as both 2.75 and 2.0 HP by iMovR.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "InMovement vs LifeSpan: which treadmill desk is better?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "It depends on width and speed. The Unsit has a 30-inch belt, a 2 mph ceiling and a lifetime frame warranty for $2,595. LifeSpan’s TX6-GlowUp has a 20-inch belt, 6 mph, the same 400 lb rating and a seven-hour daily-use figure for $1,399. For most desk walkers the LifeSpan is the better value.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Will the InMovement Unsit fit under my standing desk?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "It needs at least 40 inches between the desk legs, by InMovement’s figure, and iMovR adds a desktop of 53 inches or wider. Because it raises you 5 inches, your desk also needs to reach about 5 inches higher than your usual standing height. Measure both before ordering.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can I return an InMovement Unsit?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "InMovement offers a full refund within 30 days of delivery minus return shipping, which it says typically costs $250 to $500. The treadmill must be in new condition in its original packaging on its pallet, or a $400 to $500 repackaging charge applies. Delivery and white-glove fees are not refunded.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#shaheer-ali-khan", name: "Shaheer Ali Khan", honorificSuffix: "PhD", jobTitle: "Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist", url: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#who", sameAs: ["https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaheer-ali-khan-data/"], worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" } },
      datePublished: "2026-11-05",
      dateModified: "2026-11-05",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      brand: { "@type": "Brand", name: product.name.split(" ")[0] },
      ...(product.priceBounds
        ? {
            offers: {
              "@type": "AggregateOffer",
              priceCurrency: "USD",
              lowPrice: product.priceBounds.low,
              highPrice: product.priceBounds.high,
              url: product.amazonUrl,
            },
          }
        : {}),
    })),
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: 4,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: `https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/inmovement-treadmill-desk/#${product.id}`,
      })),
    },
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | Treadmill Reviews USA`}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-11-05",
    modifiedTime: "2026-11-05",
    author: "Shaheer Ali Khan",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "inmovement treadmill desk",
      "inmovement unsit under desk treadmill",
      "inmovement vs lifespan treadmill desk",
      "unsit standing desk",
      "inmovement unsit bundle",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "See the Range", link: "#what-inmovement-sells" }}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="bg-gray-900 py-16 lg:py-24 relative overflow-hidden">
      <svg class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full opacity-10" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
        <pattern id="dot-pattern-inmovementtreadmilldesk" x="0" y="0" width="24" height="24" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
          <circle cx="2" cy="2" r="1.5" fill="white"></circle>
        </pattern>
        <rect width="100%" height="100%" fill="url(#dot-pattern-inmovementtreadmilldesk)"></rect>
      </svg>
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-3 mb-6 flex-wrap">
          <span class="bg-[#FF5A1F] text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
            Brand Guide
          </span>
          <span class="bg-green-500 text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
            Updated November 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          InMovement Treadmill Desk: <span class="text-[#5AA9FF]">A Buyer’s Guide to the Unsit</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          InMovement is the small company that makes the Unsit, the 30-inch-wide office treadmill most people know from iMovR. It also sells the Unsit direct, with a standing desk of its own and a bundle price. This guide sets out what InMovement sells, what it costs on the day, how buying direct differs from buying through iMovR, which figures conflict, and how it compares with LifeSpan.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
          <a href="#short-answer" class="bg-[#FF5A1F] hover:bg-[#E64F16] text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm">
            The Short Answer
          </a>
          <a href="#direct-or-imovr" class="bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm border border-white/20">
            Direct or iMovR?
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>


    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 py-8 border-b border-gray-100">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="48" height="48" class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full" />
        <div>
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 leading-tight"><a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author" class="text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a></p>
          <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm leading-tight">Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block w-px h-8 bg-gray-200"></div>
        <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm">
          Last Updated: <strong class="text-gray-700">November 5, 2026</strong>
        </p>
        <div class="ml-auto">
          <SocialProof users="1.2k" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="not-prose my-10 bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 m-0 leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="text-gray-900">What we checked, and what we have not done.</strong> On
          5 November 2026 we read InMovement’s own store (inmovement.com): the home page, the Unsit
          Under Desk Treadmill, the Unsit Treadmill + Desk Bundle and the Unsit Standing Desk
          listings, including each one’s price, stock status, specification table, warranty,
          shipping and return terms. We compared those with iMovR’s Unsit listing on the same day,
          a hands-on review by Treadmill Review Guru (July 2024), an independent walking-pad spec
          tracker’s Unsit page (February 2026), and a June 2026 InMovement press release. InMovement
          and iMovR agree on the 30 x 40 in. walking surface, 0.3 to 2.0 mph, 5 in. step-up, 162 lb
          unit weight, 400 lb maximum user weight and the lifetime frame, 2-year parts and 1-year
          labour warranty. They disagree on the motor (2.75 HP, or 2.75 and 2.0 HP on iMovR’s page)
          and iMovR shows a three-year motor badge its warranty text does not explain; those are set
          out as conflicts and kept off the cards. LifeSpan figures were checked on LifeSpan’s store
          the same day. We searched the CPSC recall database for InMovement, iMovR, Unsit and LifeSpan
          and found no recall. We have not tested any of these machines. Prices change often. The
          Unsit is not sold on Amazon, so its buttons search Amazon for similar machines. We earn a
          commission if you buy through the Amazon links on this page; it does not change what we
          say.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>


    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-8">
      <div class="not-prose bg-orange-50 border border-orange-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mt-0 mb-3">Our Top Picks</h2>
        <ul class="list-none m-0 p-0">
          <li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 py-2 border-b border-orange-100 last:border-0">
            <span class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#FF5A1F]">The Treadmill:</span>
            <a href="#inmovement-unsit-treadmill" class="font-bold text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">InMovement Unsit Under Desk Treadmill</a>
            <a href="#inmovement-unsit-treadmill" class="ml-auto text-xs font-bold text-[#0F62FE] no-underline hover:underline">Jump to review &darr;</a>
          </li>
          <li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 py-2 border-b border-orange-100 last:border-0">
            <span class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#FF5A1F]">The Bundle:</span>
            <a href="#inmovement-unsit-bundle" class="font-bold text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">InMovement Unsit Treadmill + Desk Bundle</a>
            <a href="#inmovement-unsit-bundle" class="ml-auto text-xs font-bold text-[#0F62FE] no-underline hover:underline">Jump to review &darr;</a>
          </li>
          <li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 py-2 border-b border-orange-100 last:border-0">
            <span class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#FF5A1F]">LifeSpan Pick:</span>
            <a href="#lifespan-tx6-glowup" class="font-bold text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">LifeSpan TX6-GlowUp</a>
            <a href="#lifespan-tx6-glowup" class="ml-auto text-xs font-bold text-[#0F62FE] no-underline hover:underline">Jump to review &darr;</a>
          </li>
          <li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 py-2 border-b border-orange-100 last:border-0">
            <span class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#FF5A1F]">Cheaper LifeSpan:</span>
            <a href="#lifespan-tr1200pro-glowup" class="font-bold text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">LifeSpan TR1200Pro-GlowUp</a>
            <a href="#lifespan-tr1200pro-glowup" class="ml-auto text-xs font-bold text-[#0F62FE] no-underline hover:underline">Jump to review &darr;</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <h2 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mt-0 mb-4">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-[#FF5A1F]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4 6h16M4 12h16M4 18h7"></path></svg>
          In This Guide
        </h2>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <a href="#short-answer" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">1. InMovement Treadmill Desk: The Short Answer</a>
          <a href="#who-is-inmovement" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">2. Who Is InMovement, and How Is It Related to iMovR?</a>
          <a href="#what-inmovement-sells" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">3. What InMovement Sells, and What It Costs</a>
          <a href="#unsit-figures" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">4. The Unsit’s Figures: Agreed and Conflicting</a>
          <a href="#direct-or-imovr" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">5. Buying Direct From InMovement or Through iMovR</a>
          <a href="#desk-fit" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">6. The Desk: Height, Width and the 53-Inch Question</a>
          <a href="#inmovement-vs-lifespan" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">7. InMovement vs LifeSpan Treadmill Desk</a>
          <a href="#who-should-buy" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">8. Who Should Buy an InMovement Treadmill Desk</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">9. Frequently Asked Questions</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          If you searched for an InMovement treadmill desk, you have probably already seen the
          Unsit: a heavy, unusually wide office treadmill that tops out at 2 mph and sits under a
          standing desk all day. Most coverage presents it as an iMovR product, because iMovR sells
          it alongside its own desks. InMovement is the company that makes it, services it and,
          since 2026, sells it direct again, with a cheaper desk of its own. Which of the two you buy
          from changes the delivery fee, the return freight, the desk you get and who you talk to
          when something goes wrong. This guide sets that out, along with what the Unsit costs, what
          its sellers agree and disagree on, and whether a LifeSpan suits you better.
        </p>

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">1. InMovement Treadmill Desk: The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>InMovement makes one treadmill, the Unsit, and sells it direct at $2,595 or with
            its own standing desk for $3,215; it is the widest under desk treadmill we cover and is
            worth its price only if you will walk very slowly at a desk for most of the day.</strong>
            The 30-inch walking surface is the reason to buy it. The 2 mph ceiling, the 162 lb frame and
            the price are the reasons most people should not.
          </p>
          <p>
            Buying from InMovement rather than iMovR gets you the same treadmill at the same price on
            the day we checked, a lower inside-delivery fee, a slightly lower return-freight estimate,
            and a far cheaper desk. iMovR’s Lander is a more capable desk, with a higher reach for tall
            users, and iMovR publishes which desks fit the Unsit. Either way, InMovement handles the
            warranty and technical support.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you are weighing InMovement against LifeSpan, the honest summary is that LifeSpan’s
            TX6-GlowUp gives most of what the Unsit offers — a full-width belt, a 400 lb rating, a
            published daily-use figure — for about $1,200 less, with a higher top speed. The Unsit is
            the right choice only when the extra ten inches of width matters to you. We have not tested
            any of these machines; everything here comes from the sellers’ own pages and independent
            coverage, checked on 5 November 2026.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="who-is-inmovement" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">2. Who Is InMovement, and How Is It Related to iMovR?</h2>
<p>
            InMovement and iMovR are separate companies with similar names, and the overlap confuses
            many buyers. InMovement describes itself on its own store as a small business run by a
            husband-and-wife team, and gives customer-service hours of 9am to 5pm Central time on
            weekdays. Its Unsit ships from a warehouse in Indianapolis. It makes the Unsit treadmill,
            provides its warranty, runs its technical support and inspects returned units. In June
            2026 it announced in a press release that it was taking the Unsit to NeoCon, the office
            furniture trade show, for the first time, aiming it at commercial and shared workspaces.
          </p>
          <p>
            iMovR is a long-established seller of standing desks and treadmill desks. It used to sell
            its own treadmill, the ThermoTread GT, which it discontinued; the Unsit replaced it. iMovR’s
            Unsit page says plainly that InMovement provides the warranty, the technician servicing and
            customer technical support, gives an InMovement support address, and says returned units are
            inspected by InMovement before iMovR issues a refund. So when you buy an Unsit from iMovR,
            iMovR is the retailer and InMovement is the manufacturer behind it.
          </p>
          <p>
            Two small details on InMovement’s own pages show how tangled the branding is. A product image
            on the Unsit listing shows the logo as “UNiSIT by iMovement”, which matches neither company’s
            name. And the independent tracker we read, writing in February 2026, reported that older
            InMovement spec links were dead and that the Unsit was routed through iMovR. On 5 November
            2026 InMovement’s own store was live and selling the treadmill, a desk, a bundle, a standing
            stool and replacement parts. If you have read elsewhere that the Unsit is only available from
            iMovR, that is no longer the case.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our <a href="/imovr-unsit-treadmill-desk/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">review of the iMovR Unsit bundle</a>
            covers the treadmill paired with iMovR’s Lander desk in detail. This page is about the
            brand and the buying decision: what InMovement sells, and where to buy it.
          </p>
        </div>

